    Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: hamoa/x1: Fix TODO in system power domain node
    Author:  Daniel J Blueman <daniel@quora.org>
    Date:    2026-02-21
    Msg-ID:  <20260221105245.19328-1-daniel@quora.org>
    State:   Changes Requested
    Link:    https://patchwork.kernel.org/project/linux-arm-msm/patch/20260221105245.19328-1-daniel@quora.org/

Wires up the system-level PSCI power domain idle state ("DRIPS"), without
which the SoC never enters AOSS deep sleep / CX collapse / DDR self-refresh
during suspend. Verified locally via /sys/kernel/debug/qcom_stats: aosd,
cxsd and ddr counters sit at 0 across every suspend on the stock tree.

Open review points (why this is not upstream yet):
  - Maulik Shah: entry/exit latency math disagrees with the ACPI _LPI values
    (9000us total vs 5000us); Fixes: tag risks a stable backport landing
    without PDC GPIO IRQ config, which would break GPIO wakeups.
  - Bjorn Andersson: drop the Fixes: tag, this is missing functionality
    rather than a regression.
  - Konrad Dybcio (on Val Packett's earlier attempt): latencies were copied
    from a phone SoC and are not validated for laptop-class parts.

We carry it here to gather test data on x1p42100 (purwa), which neither
upstream submitter has -- both tested on x1e80100 (hamoa) parts.

Original commit message follows.
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

At present, designs based on the Qualcomm X1 Hamoa reference platform have an always-on system power domain since the OF node values aren't implement.

Fix this by using the CPU C4, cluster CL5 and system DRIPS parameters from the ACPI DSDT Windows uses, together with the Low Power Idle _LPI minimum residency of 9000us and wake latency of 5000us as exit latency. Finally, assume the entry latency is the difference of these two values.

Tested on a Lenovo Yoga Slim 7x with Qualcomm X1E-80-100.

Fixes: f33767e3cfa5 ("arm64: dts: qcom: x1e80100: Add missing system-wide PSCI power domain")
Signed-off-by: Daniel J Blueman <daniel@quora.org>

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/hamoa.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/hamoa.dtsi
index a17900eacb20..64338769bc85 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/hamoa.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/hamoa.dtsi
@@ -290,6 +290,14 @@ cluster_cl5: cluster-sleep-1 {
 				exit-latency-us = <4000>;
 				min-residency-us = <7000>;
 			};
+
+			domain_ss3: domain-sleep-0 {
+				compatible = "domain-idle-state";
+				arm,psci-suspend-param = <0x0200c354>;
+				entry-latency-us = <4000>;
+				exit-latency-us = <5000>;
+				min-residency-us = <9000>;
+			};
 		};
 	};
 
@@ -448,7 +456,7 @@ cluster_pd2: power-domain-cpu-cluster2 {
 
 		system_pd: power-domain-system {
 			#power-domain-cells = <0>;
-			/* TODO: system-wide idle states */
+			domain-idle-states = <&domain_ss3>;
 		};
 	};
 
